 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** The validation step is $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of LUT entries. The CDF computation is also $O(N)$. The upload is $O(N)$ memory bandwidth bound [G].
+*   **Time Complexity:** The validation step is $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of LUT entries [G]. The CDF computation is also $O(N)$ [G]. The upload is $O(N)$ memory bandwidth bound [G].
 *   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N)$ for the LUT storage on the GPU [G].
-*   **Performance:** The SSBO approach allows for dynamic updates and complex indexing in shaders. The texture approach is standard for hardware-accelerated interpolation [G]. The CDF check is required for DDA optimizations [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Supports dynamic transfer function updates. Handles non-monotonic inputs via CDF correction. Compatible with both SSBO and Texture-based sampling [G].
-*   **Limitations:** Requires a full upload if the TF changes. The CDF correction may alter the visual appearance of the transfer function if not carefully calibrated [S2, unofficial].
